@prefix oa:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rml:     <http://semweb.mmlab.be/ns/rml#> .
@prefix rr:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/r2rml#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xrr:     <http://i3s.unice.fr/xr2rml#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix zoo:     <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/zoo#> .


<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e>
      a       zoo:Oeuvre ;
      zoo:author "EUCHERIUS" ;
      zoo:date "2026-08-30" ;
      zoo:editor "Unknown editor" ;
      zoo:file "./zoo/zoo18/1e.xml" ;
      zoo:identifier "formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae" ;
      zoo:title "Formulae spiritalis intellegentiae" .


<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/26/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/26> ;
      zoo:text "The lion is the Lord: the lion from the tribe of Judah conquers; again in another part: let the lion seize my soul at any time." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/56/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/56> ;
      zoo:text "The flocks are the simple ones who have been plundered less of rationality than of keenness; in Solomon: feed the animals of your flock." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/41/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/41> ;
      zoo:text "The fox is a heretic or the devil or a shrewd sinner; in the gospel: go, tell that fox." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/58/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/58> ;
      zoo:text "The nanny-goats are the just who come from the gentiles; in Solomon: your long hair is like a herd of she-goats, which have appeared in Gilead." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/24/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/24> ;
      zoo:text "The fly is the devil; in Solomon: the flies of death have exterminated the oil of sweetness." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/43/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/43> ;
      zoo:text "The beasts of burden lack understanding and intelligence; in the psalm: and I have become the beasts of burden before you." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/39/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/39> ;
      zoo:text "The rabbit is one who fears God; in the psalm: the rocks are a refuge for the hares and the hedgehogs." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/11/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/11> ;
      zoo:text "The partridge is the devil; in the prophet: the partridge has cried, it has gathered that which it has not sown." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/60/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/60> ;
      zoo:text "The kids are sinners; in the gospel: the kids, however, are on the left." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/15/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/15> ;
      zoo:text "The hawk, however, is a saint, so I think, seizing the Kingdom of God; in Job: is not the hawk plumed in Your wisdom?" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/6/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/6> ;
      zoo:text "The chicks are the saints; in the psalm as above, and in a bad part of Solomon: and let the fledgelings of eagles devour him." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/30/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/30> ;
      zoo:text "The stag is Christ, or the saints; as a deer longs for the streams of water." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/8/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/8> ;
      zoo:text "The ostrich is a heretic, or a philosopher, because they do not fly with the wings of their wisdom; in Isaiah: and he will be a resting place for the dragon and a pasture for the ostrich." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/13/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/13> ;
      zoo:text "The turtledove is the Holy Spirit or the blessed man or spiritual intelligence; in the Song of Songs: the voice of the turtle was heard in our land. But then the dove is said to be the Holy Spirit; the context of many holy scriptures asserts it: then turtledove is understood to be the Holy Spirit in truth, when high scriptures or hidden mysteries are brought up." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/62/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/62> ;
      zoo:text "The dog is the devil or Judas or a gentile; in the psalm: and my only life from the hand of the dog. And in another part in Ecclesiastes: a living dog is better than a dead lion. Here they think that the lion is the devil, the dog is a true gentile or a man accepting a sinner because one can come to faith or repentance, while the other cannot." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/28/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/28> ;
      zoo:text "The elephant is a great sinner; in Kings: and they led apes and elephants to Solomon." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/45/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/45> ;
      zoo:text "The mule is an irrational man; in the psalm: do not wish to become like the horse and the mule who do not understand." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/19/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/19> ;
      zoo:text "The hen is wisdom or the church or the soul; in the gospel: as a hen gathers her chicks beneath her wings." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/63/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/63> ;
      zoo:text "The frogs are demons; in the Apocalypse: and I saw three unclean spirits in the form of frogs come from the mouth of a dragon; they were the spirits of demons. Frogs are also heretics, who do not cease to babble at a meal with vain talkativeness as they dwell in the most vile bodily feelings." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/1/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/1> ;
      zoo:text "The birds are the saints, because they fly to the higher heart; in the gospel: and he made great branches that the birds of the air might live in their shade." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/32/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/32> ;
      zoo:text "The boar is the devil; in the psalm: the boar has driven him from the forest." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/3/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/3> ;
      zoo:text "The wings are the two testaments; in Ezekiel: your body will fly with two wings of its own." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/17/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/17> ;
      zoo:text "The sparrow sometimes is the Lord or a holy man; in the psalm: indeed the sparrow has found itself a home. And it is another sparrow that is like a holy man: flying across the mountain like a sparrow." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/20/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/20> ;
      zoo:text "Bats are considered portents of the idols of darkness; in the prophet: that you may love moles and bats." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/5/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/5> ;
      zoo:text "The nest is the church, the high peace of the blessed; in the psalm: and the turtledove is in its nest where it places its chicks. And likewise, a good conscience is a nest, in which the fetus of good thoughts is cherished and it is born in good works, that they may be called children afterward; in the psalm: your children are like a new olive around your table." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/34/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/34> ;
      zoo:text "The rhinoceros is strength, either in a good or bad part; in the book of Job, according to the Hebrews: whether the rhinoceros wishes to serve you." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/65/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/65> ;
      zoo:text "The worm is Christ, who took human flesh in humility; in the psalm: I am a worm, not a man. The same in another part of Isaiah: the worm will not kill them, that is either the worm itself or the knowledge of sin." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/48/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/48> ;
      zoo:text "The camel is the wealth of a burdened age or the deformation of the dead; in the gospel: it is easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for the wealthy to enter into the kingdom of the heavens." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/51/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/51> ;
      zoo:text "The cows are those full of fleshly faults; in the psalm: among the cows of the people." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/67/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/67> ;
      zoo:text "The snake is the devil or bad men; in the gospel: snakes are the equals of vipers. The same in another part of the gospel: as Moses raised the snake in the wilderness." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/69/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/69> ;
      zoo:text "The scorpion is the devil or his ministers; in the gospel: I gave you power to crush snakes and scorpions." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/38/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/38> ;
      zoo:text "The antelope is the same as above." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/36/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/36> ;
      zoo:text "The wild ass is a hermit; in Job: who sets the wild ass free? He can, and I have said that the tribe of Judah is that wild ass, and as follows in the same book: and who has loosed his bonds? The bonds likewise are the law." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/53/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/53> ;
      zoo:text "The pigs are unclean sinners; in the epistle of Peter: the pig is washed by rolling in the mud." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/22/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/22> ;
      zoo:text "The locusts are the people; in the gospel: his food, moreover, was locusts." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/40/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/40> ;
      zoo:text "The hedgehog is as above; and the hedgehogs are a weak nation, who make their homes among the rocks." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/70/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/70> ;
      zoo:text "The vipers are the same as above; in the gospel: snakes are the equals of vipers." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/10/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/10> ;
      zoo:text "The crow is the black of the sinner or of the demons; in Solomon: the crows tore him from the valleys. The same in a good part of the Song of Songs about the spouse: his hair that is passing away is black like the crow." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/57/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/57> ;
      zoo:text "The goats are the sinners or the gentiles; in Daniel: behold, a male goat among the she-goats came from the west over the face of the whole land. The same in a good part: I offer you cows with goats." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/55/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/55> ;
      zoo:text "The sheep are the faithful people; in the gospel: my sheep hear my voice." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/27/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/27> ;
      zoo:text "The leopard is the devil, or the untrustworthy sinner in death; in the prophet: as an Ethiopian cannot change his skin nor a leopard his spots." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/9/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/9> ;
      zoo:text "The pelican is the Lord Jesus Christ in his passion or the holy man given to solitude; in the psalm: I have become solitary like a pelican." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/12/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/12> ;
      zoo:text "The dove is the Holy Spirit; in the gospel: and I saw the spirit of God descending like a dove. The same in another part: in Ephraim, a dove without feeling, without a heart." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/25/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/25> ;
      zoo:text "The wild animals are the devil or wild men; in the psalm: you do not take the wild beasts into your trust." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/42/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/42> ;
      zoo:text "The beast is the man of flesh; in the apostle: the man of flesh does not see those who are in the spirit of God." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/44/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/44> ;
      zoo:text "The horse is a holy man; in Habakkuk: he who has risen above your horses; and in a bad part: a deceitful horse into safety." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/46/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/46> ;
      zoo:text "The ass is the human body or the people of the gentiles; in the gospel: and they led an ass and its colt to Jesus and they made him sit on the colt." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/61/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/61> ;
      zoo:text "The moles are idols, or heretics, who do not see the truth; in Isaiah: that you may worship moles and bats." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/31/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/31> ;
      zoo:text "The wolf is the devil or heretics; in the gospel: the wolves are inherently rapacious. The same in a good part: Benjamin, meaning the Apostle Paul, is a ravening wolf." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/59/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/59> ;
      zoo:text "The lambs are Christ, or the apostles, or the saints; in the gospel: feed my lambs." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/29/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/29> ;
      zoo:text "The bear is the devil, or the barbarian leaders; in Kings: two bears were brought forth and they ate them." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/7/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/7> ;
      zoo:text "The eagles are the saints; in the gospel: where a body will be, there shall the eagles gather. And in a bad part: let the fledgelings of eagles devour him." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/14/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/14> ;
      zoo:text "The kite signifies, so I think, rapacity or pride; in the psalm, according to the Hebrew: the kite, once away, is at home." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/33/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/33> ;
      zoo:text "The tiger is effeminate arrogance; in the book of Job, according to the Hebrews: the tiger dies because it has no prey." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/49/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/49> ;
      zoo:text "The bulls are the leaders of the people; in the psalm: the fat bulls surrounded me." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/2/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/2> ;
      zoo:text "Flying is the death of the saints in God or the knowledge of the Scriptures; in the psalm: I shall fly and I shall be at rest." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/64/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/64> ;
      zoo:text "The ant is prudent and hard-working; in Solomon: go to the ant, o sluggard." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/18/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/18> ;
      zoo:text "The cock is the Lord, so I think, or a saint: in Solomon: and the cock is glad as it walks among the hens. And in Job: who gave the cock knowledge? And in another part: and I shall cause you to be carried off as domestic poultry is carried away." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/35/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/35> ;
      zoo:text "The one-horned is the unicorn; in the psalm: and my beloved son is like a unicorn, that is, of unique power, or unique among the saints, who wholly keep the word of God. And in another part: and my humility is like the horn of a unicorn. The unicorns having this magnificence or one testimony." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/47/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/47> ;
      zoo:text "The female ass is a circle of bystanders, or a people who lack acquaintance with God; in the gospel: the same as above." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/4/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/4> ;
      zoo:text "The feathers are the Scriptures; in the psalm: the wings of the silver dove." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/50/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/50> ;
      zoo:text "The oxen are the apostles, who take on the yoke of Christ, the gospel, the ploughshare with which they plow the world; in the psalm: I offer to you my oxen with my goats." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/16/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/16> ;
      zoo:text "The owl is Christ, or the saint who despises infidels; in the psalm: I am made like an owl in its dwelling." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/68/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/68> ;
      zoo:text "The dragon is the devil, or the overt tormenter; in the psalm: you have broken the head of the dragons, you have given him to the people of Ethiopia for food." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/21/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/21> ;
      zoo:text "The beetle in the prophet: and the beetle will cry from the wood, so I think, this means from the wood of the Lord (the cross)." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/37/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/37> ;
      zoo:text "The fawn is Christ, or the saint because of the multiplicity of his graces; in Solomon: my little brother, you are like a little antelope or like the fawn of a deer." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/66/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/66> ;
      zoo:text "The spider is human frailty; in the psalm: you have made his soul to wither like a spider." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/52/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/52> ;
      zoo:text "The calf is Christ, or the saints; in the psalm: there they shall place calves upon your altar. And in another part: many calves surrounded me, here it is poetic license." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/54/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/54> ;
      zoo:text "The rams are the apostles or the leaders of the church; in the psalm: bring the sons of rams to the Lord." .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/23/text/1>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 1 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/EUCHERIUS/formulae_spiritalis_intellegentiae/e/23> ;
      zoo:text "The bees are the stamp of virginity or of wisdom; in Solomon: go to the bee and learn how to be a worker; and in a bad part of the prophet: and the bee which is in Assyria." .


